{"w":2400,"h":2857,"lines":[{"y":0.051938898492235763,"t":"Reading","x":0.84214724227184468,"w":0.071875324249267569,"h":0.01958388161041924,"c":1},{"w":0.26124567667643228,"c":1,"x":0.19031141761459669,"y":0.101744186117666,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.015988371937820545},{"h":0.020367145872015935,"c":1,"y":0.13953488339185449,"x":0.19031142219098532,"t":"You should spend 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","w":0.66262975056966145},{"t":"Passage 3 below.","h":0.017566968545453254,"w":0.14359862009684246,"x":0.19031141649004032,"c":1,"y":0.1584302322653578},{"w":0.55749374389648443,"h":0.031764823961624944,"t":"The Globemakers: The Curious Story of","y":0.19681907422308609,"c":1,"x":0.27313756822055363},{"t":"an Ancient Craft","x":0.4359861628810025,"h":0.023442967109867041,"c":1,"y":0.22953114089563931,"w":0.23183390299479162},{"h":0.021777935842269835,"w":0.42755915323893229,"x":0.33552848416067244,"c":1,"t":"A review of Peter Bellerby's book The Globemakers","y":0.27182624061301164},{"w":0.70771657307942704,"t":"In 2008, Peter Bellerby, who lived in London, wanted to give his father a model globe","h":0.020563018830861868,"c":1,"x":0.18679659987858108,"y":0.30949222680537503},{"h":0.019525995114368588,"c":1,"t":"tor his eightieth birthday. What seemed simple enough to start with triggered an","y":0.32935500900788539,"x":0.18678214923817979,"w":0.6696711222330729},{"y":0.34883720937368157,"t":"almost obsessive, decade-long journey, marked by a series ot obstacles that would","x":0.18858130485028862,"w":0.68166091918945315,"h":0.016103308713043996,"c":1},{"y":0.36322139481033533,"c":1,"h":0.021012117347156689,"x":0.18678181459027218,"t":"have deterred anyone less determined. It ended with his establishing the world's only","w":0.70602656046549472},{"t":"bespoke globemaking company.","w":0.27162630716959635,"y":0.38372092994371398,"x":0.18858130993539893,"h":0.017608671275112786,"c":1},{"y":0.41858512771846612,"h":0.021860926196323294,"w":0.70088160196940097,"c":1,"t":"The first surprise in The Globemakers, Bellerby's account of this impulsive enterprise,","x":0.18848647616661471},{"w":0.68858133951822909,"t":"is that obtaining such a globe was not simply a matter of a quick online order and a","h":0.017441861023846039,"c":1,"x":0.18685119862595154,"y":0.43895348808951007},{"t":"repressed sigh at the shipping costs. After all, contrary to stubbornly held popular","x":0.18679594179692136,"y":0.45613520078424585,"h":0.021407441712493536,"w":0.67830388387044271,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.47265763640086178,"t":"views of our ancestors' geographical ignorance, we have known that the world is","w":0.66802856445312497,"h":0.023265747860480634,"x":0.18674451322924274},{"c":1,"w":0.6885813395182292,"x":0.18685119861819222,"t":"spherical since at least the 6th century BCE. The ancient Greek philosopher Plato in","y":0.49265220459860659,"h":0.018975702343160483},{"y":0.51009784047438311,"t":"his work Phaedo likened it to a leather ball, while the accolade of producing the first","w":0.69740422566731763,"h":0.021966946216794181,"c":1,"x":0.18676041806357963},{"x":0.18679877675136766,"c":1,"y":0.52963230875803491,"t":"recorded globe goes to the ancient Greek philosopher Crates of Mallus, who is said","h":0.020084868952308654,"w":0.6921369425455729},{"x":0.18679268533544188,"h":0.02083919330273909,"c":1,"y":0.54788043173466339,"t":"to have made one in around 150 BCE. Surely, Bellerby reasoned, a good-quality globe","w":0.71290807088216146},{"x":0.18666217130107546,"t":"wouldn't be difficult to find.","y":0.56420501919373722,"w":0.23234036763509117,"h":0.020210832711947901,"c":1},{"h":0.01891569160263884,"w":0.69377161661783859,"t":"Nearly two millennia later, however, it seemed that the art of globemaking had been","x":0.18858131945119982,"c":1,"y":0.60319767444232142},{"x":0.18506201666521369,"t":"largely forgotten. Bellerby came across shoddy commercial versions designed for","y":0.62069406747719547,"w":0.67139216105143229,"c":1,"h":0.020480488295985477},{"t":"school classrooms and genuine antiques in auction houses that would have bust his","x":0.18507859581016362,"h":0.020205051269958307,"w":0.68694254557291667,"c":1,"y":0.63939943692660617},{"x":0.18677896879145975,"y":0.65792234857484211,"h":0.02041897930575054,"c":1,"t":"budget. Even his trips to Morocco and India, where surely the knowledge of artisan","w":0.68525049845377606},{"t":"cartographers* had been preserved, drew a blank.","h":0.018965530929405228,"x":0.18685121619668627,"y":0.67732558142141697,"w":0.41695500691731763,"c":1},{"y":0.71366279072521588,"w":0.6885813395182292,"c":1,"h":0.019017405072820126,"t":"Not one to be easily thwarted, Bellerby decided to make his own good-quality globe.","x":0.18685119862612187},{"x":0.18512110374805141,"w":0.69204152425130205,"h":0.019069279216235135,"c":1,"t":"In the process, almost everything that could possibly go wrong did so. Even the shape","y":0.73093072051653252},{"t":"of the Earth posed a problem, as it is not quite a perfect sphere, but oblate (slightly","x":0.18503602324112051,"y":0.74854676847153556,"h":0.022615199159124355,"c":1,"w":0.67147557576497396},{"t":"flattened at the poles). Having decided to compromise and opt for two half-spherical","y":0.76741666798372954,"w":0.68521916707356767,"x":0.18506248503483297,"h":0.020168130926688788,"c":1},{"h":0.020836674641528496,"t":"pieces that could be fitted together, he was unable to discover anyone capable of casting","x":0.18507524734846525,"y":0.78569881350088433,"c":1,"w":0.71811284383138019},{"h":0.017565951470814856,"w":0.71107264200846354,"t":"moulds with sufficient accuracy to ensure that he would not be left with two half-spheres","y":0.80510846741009767,"x":0.185121118331002,"c":1},{"x":0.18506033345548323,"w":0.71118784586588546,"t":"that were not quite the same circumference. Even after he eventually resolved this issue,","y":0.8229945425279952,"h":0.020058968919736686,"c":1},{"y":0.84124221836240987,"w":0.71981394449869796,"x":0.18507763110441525,"t":"extracting these from the moulds resulted in piles of cracked plaster of Paris** and clouds","h":0.020560957986712869,"c":1},{"t":"of choking dust in the workshop he had set up at the rear of his house.","x":0.18505999116195795,"y":0.85895437853308754,"w":0.56933888753255213,"h":0.020437324689434044,"c":1},{"w":0.40668998718261717,"h":0.013303117371673223,"y":0.91565181565302445,"t":"* cartographer: someone involved in the science or practice of drawing maps","c":1,"x":0.1850583453032334},{"c":1,"w":0.65232844034830728,"t":"** plaster of Paris: a quick-setting plaster consisting of a fine white powder that hardens when moistened and allowed to dry","x":0.18508298151340663,"y":0.92940940920752591,"h":0.013928047671361465},{"c":1,"t":"89","h":0.013081395100512871,"y":0.9549418605347727,"x":0.88235294154541222,"w":0.022491348584492976}]}